cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BioLab Play: an interactive biomechanics laboratory for students and curious clinicians"
message: "If you use BioLab Play in teaching or research, please cite it, and cite the underlying datasets separately."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wilczynski
    given-names: Bartosz
repository-code: "https://github.com/BartWil/forfun"
url: "https://bartwil.github.io/forfun/"
abstract: >-
  Browser-based interactive experiments that teach how biomechanical numbers are
  created, manipulated and misinterpreted. Each station carries a scientific
  contract stating what was measured, what was calculated, what was modelled, and
  what may not be concluded. Covers gait, inverse dynamics, muscle mechanics,
  measurement standards and EMG signal processing, in English and Polish.
keywords:
  - biomechanics
  - gait analysis
  - electromyography
  - inverse dynamics
  - science education
  - measurement literacy
  - open educational resources
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/BartWil/forfun/blob/main/LICENSE"
